What happens: The IP packet is wrapped inside an Ethernet / Wi-Fi header and trailer.

What gets added:

Source MAC Address: Your laptop's physical Wi-Fi chip address.

Destination MAC Address: Your local router's physical MAC address (the next immediate hop on the wire).

FCS / Trailer (Frame Check Sequence): An error-checking code to verify no radio interference corrupted the data mid-air.

The Analogy: Loading the FedEx box onto a specific local Delivery Van tagged with the license plate of your house and the license plate of the local depot.
